---
.title = "Environment variables",
.description = "Configure model access, proxies, reporting, and diagnostics for ZML and LLMD.",
.date = .date("2026-11-16T00:00:00"),
.layout = "content.shtml",
---
Set these variables in the environment of the process that loads the model or
initializes the backend. The defaults refer to the ZML revision used in the
[ZML quickstart]($link.page('zml/quickstart')) and the source snapshot covered
by the [LLMD CLI reference]($link.page('llmd/cli')).

# [Pass variables to Docker]($heading.id('pass-variables-to-docker'))

Put `-e NAME` before the image name to copy an exported host value into the
container. If that variable is absent from the invoking environment, Docker
leaves it unset in the container. For example, enable **Forward HF_TOKEN** in
the [LLMD quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart').unsafeRef('lfm3-fp8-cuda'))
for a Docker launch when the model repository requires authentication. Keep
credential values out of command examples and logs.

File and directory values must use paths visible to the process. For example,
to use a gcloud application default credentials file with LLMD in Docker,
add these options before the image name and replace the host path.

```sh
--mount type=bind,source=/absolute/path/to/adc.json,target=/run/gcs-adc.json,readonly \
-e GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/run/gcs-adc.json
```

See [Docker environment options](https://docs.docker.com/reference/cli/docker/container/run/#env)
and [bind mounts](https://docs.docker.com/engine/storage/bind-mounts/).

# [Model storage and credentials]($heading.id('model-storage-and-credentials'))

| Storage | Variable | Default or precedence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Hugging Face | `HF_TOKEN` | An explicit value takes precedence, including an empty string. When unset, the loader checks `$HOME/.cache/huggingface/token`, then uses anonymous access if no token is available. |
| S3 | `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | The loader uses both keys to sign requests. If either is unset, requests are anonymous. |
| S3 | `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL`, `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3` | The first set value wins in this order. When both are unset, the endpoint is `https://s3.amazonaws.com`. |
| S3 | `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` | The first set value wins in this order. When both are unset, the region is `us-east-1`. |
| Google Cloud Storage | `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` | When set, the loader tries that file. When unset, it tries `$HOME/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json` on Linux and macOS. With no usable file, it can try GCE metadata, then anonymous access. |

Use `hf://org/repo` for a Hugging Face checkpoint. The loader defaults to the
`main` revision. Use `hf://org/repo@revision` to select a revision. For ZML,
`bazel run //tools/hf -- auth login` writes the token file. Use `s3://` and
`gs://` for the corresponding object stores.

The S3 loader reads the explicit access-key pair. Use a local checkpoint
mount if your setup requires an AWS session token. The GCS loader supports
authorized-user application default credentials and GCE metadata. Service
account key refresh is unimplemented in the reviewed snapshot.

See the pinned ZML loaders for
[Hugging Face](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/vfs/hf.zig),
[S3](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/vfs/s3.zig),
and [GCS](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/vfs/gcs.zig).

# [LLMD outbound proxies]($heading.id('llmd-outbound-proxies'))

LLMD initializes an HTTP client for remote model access. With the reviewed
Zig 0.17.1 toolchain, the first nonempty proxy value in each row wins.

| Traffic | Precedence | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| HTTP | `http_proxy`, `HTTP_PROXY`, `all_proxy`, `ALL_PROXY` | Direct connection |
| HTTPS | `https_proxy`, `HTTPS_PROXY`, `all_proxy`, `ALL_PROXY` | Direct connection |

The precedence applies to LLMD's model-loading client. Bazel's dependency
downloads and Docker's image pulls use their own proxy settings.

# [LLMD reporting controls]($heading.id('llmd-reporting-controls'))

| Variable | Default and effect |
| --- | --- |
| `DO_NOT_TRACK` | Unset unless configured. `DO_NOT_TRACK=1` disables crash reporting and usage statistics. |
| `LLMD_NO_USAGE_STATS` | Unset unless configured. `LLMD_NO_USAGE_STATS=1` disables usage statistics. |

Reporting configuration can vary by package. The reviewed source requires
`SENTRY_DSN` to enable crash reporting and both `LLMD_USAGE_STATS_ENDPOINT`
and `LLMD_POSTHOG_TOKEN` to enable usage statistics. Maintainers can override
the packaged crash handler path with `LLMD_SENTRY_HANDLER_PATH`. See the
[LLMD release notes](https://zml.ai/posts/llmd-20261106.0/) for the reporting
controls documented for that release.

# [Runtime diagnostics]($heading.id('runtime-diagnostics'))

| Variable | Default and effect |
| --- | --- |
| `ZML_AUTOTUNE_CACHE_DIR` | Unset. Selects the per-fusion autotune cache directory for CUDA, ROCm, and oneAPI. For persistence in Docker, point it to a writable mounted directory. |
| `XLA_FLAGS` | Uses the selected backend's defaults when unset. Pass supported compiler flags for the plugin shipped with your build. |
| `TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL` | `3` in the pinned ZML platform setup. Sets the compiler runtime log threshold. |
| `SKIP_PJRT_PROFILER` | Unset. `true` skips nested backend profiling and keeps local host tracing. |
| `LLMD_PROFILE_DEVICE_ONLY` | `0` when unset. `1` selects device-only tracing in LLMD. |
| `NO_COLOR`, `CLICOLOR_FORCE` | Unset by default. A nonempty `NO_COLOR` disables logo color and takes precedence over `CLICOLOR_FORCE`. A nonempty `CLICOLOR_FORCE` requests color. |
| `COLORTERM`, `TERM` | Supplied by the terminal. Used to select the logo's color depth. |
| `BUILD_WORKING_DIRECTORY` | Set by `bazel run` to the caller's working directory. The ZML LLM example uses it to resolve relative paths. |

On a plugin that supports HLO dumps, set
`XLA_FLAGS="--xla_dump_to=/path/to/dumps --xla_dump_hlo_as_text"` before
launching. Choose a writable output directory inside the runtime. See the
[OpenXLA HLO dump guide](https://openxla.org/xla/hlo_dumps).

# [Backend-specific settings]($heading.id('backend-specific-settings'))

| Backend | Variable | Default or use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| CUDA | `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` | Supplied by the host or image. The ZML loader checks it for library paths during CUDA diagnostics. |
| ROCm | `ROCPROFILER_LOG_LEVEL` | `error` when unset. Controls profiler logging. |
| Intel oneAPI | `CCL_LOG_LEVEL` | `error` when unset. Controls collective library logging. |
| AWS Neuron | `NEURON_RT_LOG_LEVEL` | `error` when unset. Controls Neuron runtime logging. |
| AWS Neuron | `NEURON_CC_FLAGS` | Generated from the backend configuration when unset. An explicit value overrides those compiler flags. |
| Furiosa | `FURIOSA_SDK_ROOT` | Set by the pinned loader to the packaged SDK location. |

Use [Compatibility]($link.page('reference/compatibility')) to identify the
runtime and artifact before applying backend-specific settings.
